    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds `docs/research-implementation-status.md`: a codebase-wide analysis of how far `dev` (at 0943461829) realizes each major-venue Hazel paper, plus a full account of how **modules and type members** work today and how they worked in the two earlier, unmerged designs.\n\nContents:\n- Executive summary table (eleven POPL/ICFP/PLDI/OOPSLA papers, one status and one line each) and a repository-eras table.\n- Per-paper sections grouped by theme (editor calculi, dynamics, static semantics, editor services and data, collaboration/teaching), each with the paper's claims, a feature-by-feature status table with `file:line` evidence, history with commits/PRs/branches, a verdict, and key files.\n- Modules and type members: the labeled-tuple design on `dev` verified against code and by running programs through the CLI (including signature `type` entries not binding and being captured by the checked value), the 2023\u201324 first-class design (PR #1020), the 2025 gc-modules design (PR #1788), a comparison table, and what real type members would need.\n- Cross-cutting observations: mechanisms merged then removed, stale docs and dead code, a probable livelit-view regression.\n\nEverything is documentation; no code changes. Line numbers are pinned to 0943461829 and will drift.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
